# Vantora AI — environment template
#
# EVERY VARIABLE BELOW IS OPTIONAL.
#
# With an empty .env (or no .env at all) the application still runs end to end
# and all 77 tests pass:
#
#   * No DATABASE_URL  -> `seedApexDataset()` returns mode "in-memory" and serves
#                         the canonical Apex Manufacturing dataset from
#                         src/lib/sandbox/seed-data.ts. No database is needed to
#                         build, test, or demo.
#   * No Python engine -> src/lib/quant-client.ts falls back to its seeded
#                         deterministic TypeScript mirror, so the forecast and
#                         the recovery plan are still produced (the two live
#                         bridge tests skip themselves when the engine is down).
#   * No ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> the copilot answers from its deterministic
#                         narrative synthesiser. Every figure it emits is still
#                         verified against the quant engine before release.
#   * No HITL_SIGNING_SECRET -> Tier 2 operations fail closed. The gate denies
#                         them and logs the denial; nothing is ever executed
#                         with an unsigned approval.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in only what you actually want to switch on.


# ─── Database (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase PostgreSQL. Set these to persist SmeProfile / InvoiceAR / PayableAP /
# FinancingOption / RecoveryPlan / AuditLog rows instead of using the in-memory
# dataset. Then run `npm run db:push` (prisma db push && prisma generate).
#
# Prisma 7 reads these through prisma.config.ts, not the datasource block.
# DATABASE_URL is the transaction-mode pooler; DIRECT_URL is the session-mode
# pooler used for migrations.
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/postgres"


# ─── Supabase client (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed if you add browser-side Supabase calls. Nothing in the current
# code path requires them.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."


# ─── Python quantitative engine (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# Where the FastAPI MILP/Monte Carlo service listens. Defaults to
# http://127.0.0.1:8000. Start it with `npm run quant`, or both servers with
# `npm run dev:all`. If it is unreachable the TypeScript mirror takes over and
# the UI badge switches to "Deterministic TS Mirror: Active".
#
# QUANT_ENGINE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"


# ─── Copilot model (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With a key the copilot runs a real Anthropic tool-use loop over the gated
# tools; without one it uses the deterministic synthesiser. Either way the
# answer must clear verifyNumericalIntegrity before it is returned.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL="claude-opus-5-5"   # default when unset


# ─── Human-in-the-loop approval signing (recommended for the demo) ────────────
# HMAC-SHA256 secret used to mint and verify Tier 2 userApprovalTokens. Minimum
# 8 characters; use a long random value in anything resembling production.
# Unset = every Tier 2 operation is denied (fail-closed, by design).
#
# HITL_SIGNING_SECRET="change-me-to-a-long-random-string"
